 **Formulas:**
-*   **Normal Computation:** The normal $\mathbf{n}$ at a voxel center is approximated by the gradient of the scalar field $V$:
-    $$ \mathbf{n} = \nabla V = \left[ \frac{\partial V}{\partial x}, \frac{\partial V}{\partial y}, \frac{\partial V}{\partial z} \right] $$
-    [G] In practice, central differences are used for $\frac{\partial V}{\partial x}$ etc., and the result is normalized.
-*   **Edge Detection:** A first-order differential operator $D$ applied to the depth buffer $D_{buf}$:
+*   **Edge Detection:** A first-order differential operator $D$ applied to the depth buffer $D_{buf}$ yields the edge map $E$:
     $$ E = |D(D_{buf})| $$
     Pixels where $E$ exceeds a threshold are marked as edges [S1, unofficial].
