 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Aliasing:** Sharp surface borders may exhibit aliasing artifacts due to pixel discretization [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Transparency/Reflection:** The basic method assumes opaque objects. It cannot natively enhance reflected or transparent images without extensions [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Parameter Tuning:** There is no automatic way to determine the optimal combination of enhancement techniques. It requires manual trial and error based on scene context and viewer preference [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Resolution Mismatch:** If the source volume is significantly smaller than the target image, reconstruction artifacts appear. Interpolation is necessary [S1, unofficial].
