 ## Background
-The G-buffer approach was proposed by Saito and Takahashi [ST90] to enable line generation and NPR effects. It has been applied to various domains including medical imaging (e.g., CT datasets of skulls), topographical maps, and surface analysis [S1, unofficial]. The method is a foundational technique in pixel-based NPR for volume visualization, allowing for interactive user experimentation by decoupling geometry from style [S1, unofficial].
